<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ferdinand Magellan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1480–<a href="/years/1521">1521</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Fernão de Magalhães</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ferdinand Magellan was a Portuguese navigator who led a Spanish expedition from 1519 to find a western route to the Spice Islands. He passed the strait that bears his name and crossed the Pacific, reaching the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a> in 1521, where he met local rulers and was killed at Mactan. His surviving ships loaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cloves">cloves</a> at Tidore, and one completed the first circumnavigation.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ferdinand-magellan.jpg" alt="Ferdinand Magellan" width="320" height="395" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ferdinand_Magellan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
